## Level 3: Components (the service)

| component | responsibility | evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `items` | read what was proposed and decided | `tools/{{ key }}/service.py::items` |
| `propose` | record a proposal (anyone, or an agent): decides nothing | `tools/{{ key }}/service.py::propose` |
| `decide` | a person's declared step, separate from the proposer | `tools/{{ key }}/service.py::decide` |
| `twin_evidence` | what the twin observes, with threads | `tools/{{ key }}/service.py::twin_evidence` |
| telemetry | one OTel span per route and call | `tools/{{ key }}/telemetry.py` |

Level 4 (code) is the source itself; C4 draws it only where it helps, and this scaffold does not.

## Supplementary: Deployment

The service runs inside the ICDEV[IT] dashboard process, gated by `{{ env_flag }}`; it has no listener of its own.

## Supplementary: Dynamic (propose, then decide)

1. A person or an agent calls `propose` (`POST {{ url_prefix }}/api/propose`): a proposal row, nothing decided.
2. A person who is not the proposer takes the declared step (`POST {{ url_prefix }}/api/decide`), with a reason.
3. The twin adapter observes both, each finding threaded to its row.

